<%# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    THE COUNTDOWN (PASS 2 rework, lesson 29). Real engine timers; nothing here
    fails the mission. The old clock started at the briefing and ran 60 real
    minutes, VM time included, so most players watched it hit zero and then
    saved the grid anyway. Now:
      architect_t20_played    10 min after team_assigned  (he names what was left)
      architect_t10_played    40 min after team_assigned  AND redirect_window_closed
      -- the cascade is ARMED when the player logs in to the attack host (flag 3) --
      architect_t5_played     10 min after flag3_submitted
      architect_t1_played     14 min after flag3_submitted
      countdown_expired       15 min after flag3_submitted (step one runs: Seattle)
    Only the armed clock is shown. All cancelled by grid_saved.
    PASS 2 review M1: the HUD (ui/scenario-timer.js) ignores cancelOnGlobal and
    the dispatcher restarts started timers on reload, so each timer also
    carries a "condition" on grid_saved: the HUD hides a timer whose condition
    fails (scenario-timer.js:140-150) and the dispatcher skips its setGlobal
    (scenario-timer-dispatcher.js:106-120). Engine gap logged. The redirect
    window also closes on flag3_submitted (agent_0x99 mapping).
